1
00:00:00,120 --> 00:00:03,641
Right below these waves lies
an ancient drowned bridge,

2
00:00:03,661 --> 00:00:06,751
whose secret science still
cannot fully explain.

3
00:00:09,499 --> 00:00:11,777
We are going to explore Dhanushkodi,

4
00:00:11,797 --> 00:00:14,990
one of India's most
mysterious and deserted towns.

5
00:00:17,225 --> 00:00:21,916
Here, legends of the sea meet
real ruins lying under real water.

6
00:00:24,090 --> 00:00:26,365
What is actually hidden under the water?

7
00:00:28,326 --> 00:00:30,071
What still remains here today?

8
00:00:31,168 --> 00:00:35,885
After you know the truth, the way
you see Ram Setu may change forever.

9
00:00:38,431 --> 00:00:41,119
Dhanushkodi sits at
India's southern tip,

10
00:00:41,139 --> 00:00:43,450
the last edge of Rameswaram island.

11
00:00:44,918 --> 00:00:47,485
It was once a busy
port and railway town.

12
00:00:50,184 --> 00:00:54,317
From here, the train connected
straight to ships bound for Sri Lanka.

13
00:00:55,349 --> 00:01:01,016
Then, in December nineteen sixty
four, a terrible cyclone struck.

14
00:01:01,136 --> 00:01:05,616
The waves rose over the whole
town, and swept everything away,

15
00:01:05,636 --> 00:01:06,725
even the train.

16
00:01:06,845 --> 00:01:10,330
The government declared
the place unfit to live in,

17
00:01:10,350 --> 00:01:12,756
and the town was abandoned forever.

18
00:01:12,925 --> 00:01:13,711
Even today,

19
00:01:13,731 --> 00:01:18,055
a broken railway station and
church ruins still stand here.

20
00:01:18,509 --> 00:01:22,125
And right here begins
the mystery of Ram Setu.

21
00:01:23,713 --> 00:01:28,351
The Ramayana says that Shri Ram's army
built a bridge from here to Lanka.

22
00:01:29,633 --> 00:01:32,795
Today, in that very place under the sea,

23
00:01:32,815 --> 00:01:37,348
lies a long line of limestone,
also called Adam's Bridge.

24
00:01:37,796 --> 00:01:41,312
That line is about forty
eight kilometres long.

25
00:01:41,578 --> 00:01:44,195
ISRO scientists mapped it completely,

26
00:01:44,215 --> 00:01:47,635
and found it joins
Dhanushkodi to Mannar island.

27
00:01:48,921 --> 00:01:50,486
And in twenty twenty one,

28
00:01:50,506 --> 00:01:55,259
the Archaeological Survey approved a
deeper study of its age and structure.

29
00:01:56,087 --> 00:01:59,908
But whether people built it or nature
did, scientists still disagree.

30
00:02:03,053 --> 00:02:06,476
Now come back to land,
and explore Dhanushkodi.

31
00:02:06,937 --> 00:02:08,976
First, go to Arichal Munai,

32
00:02:08,996 --> 00:02:12,581
where the Bay of Bengal
meets the Indian Ocean.

33
00:02:12,722 --> 00:02:16,201
From here, the blue sea
stretches toward Ram Setu.

34
00:02:18,207 --> 00:02:21,590
Then see the broken railway
station and the church ruins.

35
00:02:22,145 --> 00:02:26,139
And in Rameswaram, visit
the Ramanathaswamy Temple.

36
00:02:27,167 --> 00:02:30,334
On the way you will cross
the new Pamban Bridge,

37
00:02:30,354 --> 00:02:32,923
India's first vertical lift sea bridge,

38
00:02:32,943 --> 00:02:35,266
opened in April twenty twenty five.

39
00:02:37,271 --> 00:02:39,173
So remember these four places,

40
00:02:40,172 --> 00:02:41,296
Arichal Munai,

41
00:02:41,692 --> 00:02:43,368
the broken railway station,

42
00:02:43,853 --> 00:02:45,040
the church ruins,

43
00:02:45,974 --> 00:02:47,571
and the Ramanathaswamy Temple.

44
00:02:48,295 --> 00:02:50,723
Now the question, how do you get there?

45
00:02:51,851 --> 00:02:54,067
The nearest big airport is Madurai,

46
00:02:54,087 --> 00:02:57,793
about one hundred seventy five
kilometres from Rameswaram.

47
00:02:59,236 --> 00:03:02,672
From Madurai to Rameswaram
takes about three hours by road.

48
00:03:03,939 --> 00:03:07,639
Direct trains also run to
Rameswaram from Chennai,

49
00:03:07,659 --> 00:03:09,444
Madurai and Kanyakumari.

50
00:03:10,083 --> 00:03:13,878
From Rameswaram, Dhanushkodi
is about eighteen kilometres,

51
00:03:13,898 --> 00:03:15,609
by government bus or jeep.

52
00:03:17,039 --> 00:03:21,587
Dhanushkodi is open only in the
daytime, so be back before evening.

53
00:03:21,963 --> 00:03:24,774
The best season to visit
is October to March.

54
00:03:26,828 --> 00:03:28,190
Now let us plan one day.

55
00:03:29,670 --> 00:03:30,621
In the morning,

56
00:03:30,641 --> 00:03:34,264
have darshan at the Ramanathaswamy
Temple in Rameswaram.

57
00:03:35,495 --> 00:03:38,181
At ten, head to
Dhanushkodi by bus or jeep.

58
00:03:40,053 --> 00:03:43,629
In the afternoon, see the
broken station and the church.

59
00:03:44,274 --> 00:03:47,850
And before evening, enjoy the
sea view at Arichal Munai.

60
00:03:49,676 --> 00:03:52,012
Carry water, a cap and sunglasses,

61
00:03:52,032 --> 00:03:54,804
because there is very little shade here.

62
00:03:56,138 --> 00:03:59,597
You walk on sand, so
wear comfortable shoes.

63
00:04:01,820 --> 00:04:05,630
The truth is, Dhanushkodi
is not just a deserted town,

64
00:04:05,650 --> 00:04:08,274
it is an unfinished story of the sea.

65
00:04:10,388 --> 00:04:15,317
Dhanushkodi sank in a storm, but
our channel must not sink, bro.

66
00:04:16,900 --> 00:04:19,657
So subscribe, and save it from drowning.
